{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The fruit of your womb.</b> The children, and 'womb' is a hint." "<b>And the fruit of your land.</b> He mentioned grain, new wine, and fresh oil, for they are the essence." "<b>Your young.</b> I have explained it." "<b>Your flocks.</b> Like אלופינו; bearing." "<b>And your herds.</b> Like flocks. And there was a great commentator in Spain, and he brought a reason why the Hebrews called cattle by the name אלף and sheep by עשתרות, and likewise he used to interpret 'and the Ashtaroth' as the master of the constellation of growth and of the tenth. And further, it is not enough that He bless the fruit of your womb, for there shall not be in you a barren person whose seed does not beget, and likewise your livestock, for they shall further be healthy from every known disease, to be as the custom of the world. <b>And all your diseases.</b> That were outside the custom."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {4 "Reading מדוי as מדוי (diseases), following the verse's כל מדוי; the phrase 'ועשתרות בעל המזל הצומח והעשירי' is obscure and rendered hyper-literally; 'the tenth' (העשירי) is textually uncertain and may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:46.497458735Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}